# Test: $include path traversal is blocked by cap-std RESOLVE_BENEATH
#
# This test verifies that attempting to use ".." in an include path to traverse
# outside the DirCap's root directory is rejected by cap-std.
#
# cap-std's Dir::open() with RESOLVE_BENEATH semantics enforces that all path
# operations stay within the directory tree rooted at the cap. Attempts to use
# ".." to escape the cap root, or absolute paths, are rejected at the kernel
# level before any file system access occurs.
#
# Security context: This mitigates CWE-22 (Path Traversal). An attacker who can
# supply a malicious .llt file cannot read arbitrary system files like
# /etc/passwd or ~/.ssh/id_rsa by opening that file in an editor with the LSP.
#
# Expected: include error (not file content).

[include %pwd "../../etc/passwd"]
=== error
[E051]
